# Skip-list for TestMRIParseTreeDiff (parsetree_test.go).
#
# Format: <phase> <version-range> <pattern>[: reason]
#
# phase   = src2-rejected | tree-mismatch
# range   = *                          (all versions)
#         | <ver>                      (single version, e.g. 3.4)
#         | <lo>..                     (lo and above)
#         | ..<hi>                     (hi and below)
#         | <lo>..<hi>                 (closed range)
# pattern = path relative to repo root; segments may be `*`
#
# Stale entries (where the test now passes) fail loudly -- prune them out.
#
# Note: this list only covers cases the test runner cannot auto-classify --
# goruby printer / parser bugs that produce src2 MRI rejects, or tree
# mismatches between src1 and src2. The runner already auto-skips ~35 (file,
# ver) cells where MRI itself rejects src1 (segfaults on older MRI, missing
# stdlib encodings like Windows-31J / EUC-JP / cp932 / shift_jis,
# stack-level-too-deep on test_rational2, --dump=parsetree quirks, etc.),
# plus a handful of MRI timeouts and one version-boundary fixture that
# intentionally tests syntax goruby does not support. None of those are
# goruby's responsibility, so they don't need explicit skip entries here.
#
# MRI 3.4-only quirk: rational-float literals with digit-group
# underscores like `0.1_2r` parse as Rational(3, 250) instead of
# Rational(3, 25). Fixed upstream in 4.0 (which agrees with goruby's
# underscore-as-separator interpretation), so the divergence is a 3.4
# parser bug we shouldn't mirror.
tree-mismatch 3.4 internal/integrationtest/testdata/mri-tests/test_literal.rb: MRI 3.4 mis-parses `0.1_2r`; fixed in 4.0
